About the Role: &nbsp;

We are seeking a highly organized, proactive, and detail-oriented Executive&nbsp;Assistant&nbsp;to support the Chief Revenue Officer (CRO) across all day-to-day activities in a dynamic, fast-paced environment. &nbsp;This role provides standard admin support to the CRO (scheduling, travel, meeting management) plus a heavy focus on managing projects, processes, and operating priorities across the team. &nbsp;The successful candidate will act as an extension of the CRO - building strong working relationships across&nbsp;the organization as a whole, anticipating needs, and connecting the dots to drive initiatives forward independently. &nbsp;

Responsibilities: &nbsp;

Strategic Calendar Management &amp; Travel &nbsp;

• Own the CRO’s calendar as a strategic asset: &nbsp;align time with business priorities, decide which meetings, escalations, and requests reach the CRO, and rebalance proactively as priorities shift. &nbsp;

• Coordinate domestic and international travel, and process expenses accurately and in line with policy, using systems and automation where possible so this doesn’t dominate the role. &nbsp;

Commercial Operating Rhythm &nbsp;

• Run the CRO’s recurring cadence: planning cycles, pipeline and forecast reviews, leadership meetings, people initiatives. &nbsp;Prepare agendas and briefings, make sure the right inputs and owners are in place, and track decisions and actions to completion. &nbsp;

• Lead or support projects on the CRO’s behalf, such as sales kickoffs,&nbsp;process improvements, product/tech updates, and reporting. &nbsp;Act as a true PM who spots risks, gaps, and opportunities, keeps projects moving, and shares updates/status proactively. &nbsp;

• Own planning and execution for all-hands meetings and leadership off-sites, including agenda design, presentation materials, budget, logistics coordination and&nbsp;follow-up. &nbsp;

Communication and Representation: &nbsp;

• Act as a trusted voice for the CRO with other Genius executives, the Commercial organization, and with external partners and clients. &nbsp;

• Draft communications,&nbsp;handle inquiries independently, and escalate only what needs the CRO’s attention. &nbsp;

• Help the CRO manage priority client and partner relationships by preparing for meetings, tracking commitments, and coordinating executive engagement. &nbsp;

• Build and use strong working relationships across the organization to remove blockers, gather context, and keep the CRO informed. &nbsp;

• Handle sensitive commercial, financial, and people information with discretion, using sound judgment on what to communicate, when, and to who. &nbsp;

Qualifications: &nbsp;

• Bachelor's degree and 6+ years of experience providing Executive level support or business partnering, ideally within a Commercial / Sales function. &nbsp;

• Prior experience working in media, technology, or related industries. &nbsp;

• Proven examples of using a forward-thinking, resourceful approach to anticipate needs and solve problems independently. &nbsp;

• Exceptional ability to manage time, multitask, and prioritize effectively under pressure. &nbsp;

• Exceptional verbal and written communication skills with a professional and diplomatic demeanor. &nbsp;

• Demonstrated ability to build trust and foster relationships across all levels of an organization. &nbsp;

• High level of accuracy, confidentiality, and attention to detail across all work. &nbsp;

• Proficient in Office 3

